        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join squares into two rectangular panels. Place both panels right sides together with the long edges aligned. Seam the top 20 cm at each end of the top edge, leaving a 20 cm neck opening in the centre. Turn right sides out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Adding the fringe"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn into 40 cm lengths. Working along both short hem edges, fold two strands in half, insert the loop through an edge stitch, draw the tails through the loop and pull snug. Space fringes every second stitch across each hem edge. Trim the fringe tails to an even length."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
